$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Cesium carbonate (3.76 g, 11.5 mmol), ethyl
6-bromo-4-{[(1R)-1-(4-chlorophenyl)ethyl]amino}-3-quinolinecarboxylate
(2.0 g, 4.6 mmol), pyridin-3-ylboronic acid (0.62 g, 5.1 mmol) and
tetrakis(triphenylphoshine)palladium(0) (266 mg, 0.23 mmol) were
dissolved in dioxane (50 mL) and water (7 mL) and heated to reflux for 2
hours . The reaction mixture was then allowed to cool to RT, and then
filtered and evaporated to dryness. The crude residue was disolved in
EtOAc (200 mL) and washed sequentially with water (2 x 50 mL), and brine
(50 mL) . The organic layer was dried over MgSO4, filtered and evaporated
to afford crude product, which was purified by FC, eluting with a
gradient of 0-10% MeOH in DCM. Pure fractions were evaporated to dryness.
Ethyl
4-{[(1R)-1-(4-chlorophenyl)ethyl]amino}-6-(3-pyridinyl)-3-quinolinecarboxylate
(1.210 g, 60.8%) 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6, 300 K) 1.37 (3H, t), 1.64
(3H, d), 4.28-4.47 (2H, m), 5.39- 5.53 (1H, m), 7.32-7.55 (5H, m),
7.76-7.90 (1H, m), 7.94 (1H, d), 8.07 (1H, dd), 8.30 (1H, d), 8.59 (1H,
dd), 8.78 (1H, d), 8.95 (1H, s), 9.20 (1H, d). m/z (ES+), 432.1 (M+H)+.
