$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A suspension of crude boronic acid S7 (ca. 0.29 mmol), bromide rac-14a
(70 mg, 0.14 mmol), sodium carbonate (31 mg, 0.29 mmol) and
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (18 mg, 0.016 mmol) in DME/water
(8/1, 1.35 mL) was heated to 110°C under microwave irradiation for 1 h.
The reaction was quenched with brine and extracted with EtOAc. The
combined organics were washed with brine, dried (Na2SO4), concentrated
and purified by Biotage column chromatography (0-5% MeOH/DCM). Pyridine
16d (49 mg, 60%). (±)-Methyl
4-(2-amino-5-(5-((dimethylamino)methyl)-4-methylthiophen-2-yl)pyridin-3-yl)-2-(1-(2-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)ethoxy)benzoate
16d HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C30H31F3N3O3S (M + H) 570.2033, found
570.2041. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.28 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H), 7.92 (d, J
= 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.87 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.67 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.57
(t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.39 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.36 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H),
7.07 (dd, J = 7.9, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 6.93 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 6.86 (s, 1H),
5.85 (q, J = 6.4 Hz, 1H), 4.37 (s, 2H), 3.99 (s, 3H), 3.57 (s, 2H), 2.34
(s, 6H), 2.21 (s, 3H), 1.74 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 3H).
