$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Step
2.N0-(3-Chloro-5-oxo-5H-benzo[4,5]cyclohepta[1,2-b]pyridin-7-yl)-N-[(2R)-1,4-dioxan-2-ylmethyl]-N-methylsulfuric
diamide (8.05 g, 17.9 mmol),
1-methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole
(11.2 g, 53.7 mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (0.820 g, 0.895 mmol), t-Bu3PHBF4 (0.520
g, 1.79 mmol), potassium fluoride (3.43 g, 59.1 mmol), and DMF (200 mL)
were combined in a dry flask. The mixture was sparged with argon for 5min
and then heated to 100 -C. After 3 h, the solution was diluted with EtOAc
and washed with saturated sodium bicarbonate,H2O, and brine. The organic
layer was dried with magnesium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was crystallized from a mixture of methanol (70 mL),
DCM (275 mL), and hexanes (600 mL) to afford 6.17 g of
N-[(2R)-1,4-dioxan-2-ylmethyl]-N-methyl-N0-[3-(1-methyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-5-oxo-5H-benzo[4,5]cyclohepta[1,2-b]-pyridin-7-yl]sulfuric
diamide (70%). Step 4 Compound 58 was prepared in analogy to 81, using
N-(3-chloro-5-oxo-5H-benzo[4,5]cyclohepta[1,2-b]pyridin-7-yl)-2-(1H-imidazol-1-yl)ethanesulfonamide
(59% yield). 1H NMR (600 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 10.57 (br s, 1H); 9.20 (d, J =
2.4 Hz, 1H); 8.55 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H); 8.47 (s, 1H); 8.14 (s, 1H); 7.98
(d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H); 7.76 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H); 7.62 (s, 1H); 7.56 (dd, J
= 8.4, 2.4 Hz, 1H); 7.33 (d, J = 12.6 Hz, 1H); 7.24 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H);
7.16 (s, 1H); 6.79 (s, 1H); 4.34 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H); 3.88 (s, 3H); 3.71
(t, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H). LRMS (ESI) calc’d for (C23H21N6O3S) [M+ H]+, 461.1;
found 461.0.
