$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A oven dried round bottom flask was charged
with anhydrous K2CO3 (0.31 mmol), phenyl boronic acid (0.18 mmol) and
Tetrakis (triphenylphosphine) palladium(0) (0.009 mmol) and 8 mL of
toluene:ethanol (4:1) and stirred for 5 min at room temperature.
N-(3-(6-bromo-3Himidazo[
4,5-b]pyridin-2-yl)-4-fluorophenyl)pyrrolidine-1-carboxamide (0.12 mmol)
described above was added and the mixture refluxed at 90° C under
nitrogen overnight. Solvent was evaporated and the crude product
dissolved in CHCl3 (50 mL) and wash with water (30 mL), saturated aq.
NaHCO3 (30 mL) and brine (30 mL). The organic layer was dried over
Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated. The crude solid product was purified
by column chromatography using 0-3.5% MeOH in CH2Cl2. 68% yield as an
off-white solid.
N-(4-fluoro-3-(6-(pyrimidin-5-yl)-3H-imidazo[4,5-b]pyridin-2-yl)phenyl)pyrrolidine-1-carboxamide
(84). Synthesized analogous to compound 64 by a reaction with
pyrimidin-5-boronic acid which yielded the titled product, column
chromatography (0-4.0% MeOH/CH2Cl2). 58% yield, colourless solid. 1H NMR
(300 MHz, MeOH-d 4): δ 9.21-9.07 (3H, m), 8.72-8.68 (1H, m), 8.27-8.18
(1H, m), 7.81-7.75 (2H, m), 7.24 (1H, t, J = 9.2 Hz), 3.49 (4H, t, J =
6.7 Hz), 1.98 (4H, t, J = 6.0 Hz); MS m/z 404.5 (M+H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Substituted 2-Phenylimidazopyridines: A New Class of Drug Leads for Human
African Trypanosomiasis
