$DATUM A degassed mixture of
N-[5-bromo-2-(methyloxy)-3-pyridinyl]-2,4-difluoro-N-methylbenzenesulfonamide
(36) (235 mg, 0.598 mmol),
4,4,4',4',5,5,5',5'-octamethyl-2,2'-bi-1,3,2-dioxaborolane (167 mg, 0.657
mmol), PdCl2(dppf)-DCM adduct (48.8 mg, 0.060 mmol), KOAc (176 mg, 1.793
mmol) in 1,4-dioxane (5 mL) was heated at 80°C. After 2 hours, the
reaction cooled to room temperature. The reaction was filtered through
Celite®, rinsing with EtOAc. The filtrate was concentrated, re-evaporated
from DCM/hexane (2x). The residue was dissolved in DCM, concentrated onto
Celite®, and purified by silica gel chromatography (0-100% EtOAc/hexane).
2,4-difluoro-N-methyl-N-[2-(methyloxy)-5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-3-pyridinyl]benzenesulfonamide
(39) (146 mg, 0.332 mmol, 55.5 % yield) as a white solid. 1H NMR (400
MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ ppm 1.26-1.35 (m, 12 H) 3.20 (d, J=1.46 Hz, 3 H) 3.58
(s, 3 H) 7.23 (td, J=8.51, 2.19 Hz, 1 H) 7.56-7.74 (m, 2 H) 7.74-7.82 (m,
1 H) 8.34 (d, J=1.76 Hz, 1 H), LC-MS m/z = 441.3 (M+H) +.
