$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-{[(1R)-1-(4-chlorophenyl)ethyl]amino}-6-(3-pyridinyl)-3-quinolinecarboxamide
(7) A mixture of
(R)-6-bromo-4-(1-(4-chlorophenyl)ethylamino)quinoline-3-carboxamide (80
mg, 0.2 mmol), pyridin-4-ylboronic acid (24.3 mg, 0.2 mmol), cesium
carbonate (64.4 mg, 0.2 mmol) and tetrakis(triphenylphoshine)palladium(0)
(228 mg, 0.2 mmol) in degassed dioxane (3.5 mL) / water (0.5 mL) mixture
were heated at 150 °C for 30 minutes in a microwave. The reaction mixture
was partitioned with EtOAc (10 mL) and the organic layer was separated,
dried over sodium sulfate. The crude product was dissloved in DMSO (2 mL)
and purified by preparative LCMC using ammonium acetate/water/MeCN
(10-80). Pure fractions were concentrated.
4-{[(1R)-1-(4-chlorophenyl)ethyl]amino}-6-(3-pyridinyl)-3-quinolinecarboxamide
(50 mg, 55%) as a colourless solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d 6, 300 K)
1.59 (3H, d, J 6.6), 5.27-5.43 (1H, m), 7.36-7.53 (6H, m), 7.90 (1H, d, J
8.8), 8.06 (1H, dd, J 8.8, 1.5), 8.19 (1H, br s), 8.35 (1H, d, J 1.5),.
8.59 (2H, d, J 5.8), 8.81 (1H, s), 9.64 (1H, d, J 7.8). HRMS (ESI+): Anal
cald for C23H20 ClN4O (M+H)+: 403.1326; Found: 403.1367.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Novel 3-Quinoline Carboxamides as Potent, Selective, and
Orally Bioavailable Inhibitors of Ataxia Telangiectasia Mutated (ATM)
Kinase
