$DATUM N-(4-((2-Amino-6-chloropyrimidin-4-yloxy)methyl)benzyl)-2-(3-methyl-4-(3-oxo-6-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-3Hxanthen-9-yl)phenoxy)acetamide,
SPG2 (12). Compound 10(25 mg, 0.051 mmol) dissolved in anhydrous DMF (2
mL) was added to a dried 5 mL round-bottom flask and the solution was
stirred at room temperature for 5 min. HATU (25 mg, 0.066 mmol), compound
3 (18 mg, 0.068 mmol), and DIPEA (25 uL) were added, and the reaction was
stirred at room temperature overnight. DMF was removed under vacuo and
the orange oil was redissolved in 10% MeOH in CH2Cl2. Purification by
flash column chromatography (silica gel, MeOH:CH2Cl2 1:10) afforded SPG2
12 as an orange film (20 mg, 0.027 mmol, 53% yield). 1H NMR (20% MeOD in
CDCl3) δ 7.92 (1H, s), 7.55 (1H, d, J = 6.4 Hz), 7.33 (2H, d, J = 6.4
Hz), 7.28 (2H, d, J = 6.4 Hz), 7.07 (1H, d, J = 6.8 Hz), 7.02 (1H, d, J =
6.4 Hz), 6.90-7.00 (3H, m), 6.58 (1H, d, J = 7.6 Hz), 6.43 (1H, s), 6.06
(1H, s), 5.26 (2H, s), 4.61 (2H, s), 4.53 (2H, d, J = 3.6 Hz), 1.98 (3H,
s), 1.32 (12H, s). ESI-MS: calculated for [MH+] 733.25, found 733.26.
