$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A solution of 1a (77 mg, 0.2 mmol), 2a (162
mg, 0.4 mmol), Pd(PPh34 (138 mg, 0.12 mmol) and K2CO3 (276 mg, 2 mmol) in
THF (4 mL) and water (2 mL) was degassed by 6 freeze-pump- thaw cycles.
Then the mixture was heated at 70 ° C for 12h. TLC showed the
disappearance of the starting material 2a. After cooling down to room
temperature, the mixture was diluted with dichloromethane (50 mL). The
organic layer was dried over sodium sulfate and evaporated under reduced
pressure to give a brown solid. The crude product was purified using
column chromatography (SiO2, 230-400 meshes) with CH2Cl2 /hexanes/ethyl
acetate (100/100/5) as eluents. Compound no. 3ab (Yield: 50%). Mp:
241-243 °C. 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ = 8.72 (d, J= 8 Hz, 2 H), 8.63 (t,
J= 8.8 Hz, 4 H), 8.17 (s, 4 H), 8.07 (d, J= 8.4 Hz, 2 H), 7.88 (s, 2 H),
7.74 - 7.51 (m, 18 H), 6.71 (d, J= 7.6 Hz, 2 H), 5.76 (s, 2 H), 2.85 (s,
6 H), 1.49 (s, 12 H).13C NMR (CDCl3) δ = 151.03, 150.02, 147.28, 139.27,
137.97, 136.91, 132.54, 132.31, 131.35, 130.88, 130.33, 129.89, 127.71,
127.46, 127.37, 127.15, 126.70, 126.42, 126.07, 125.67, 124.96,124.89,
124.21, 122.66, 122.45, 122.15, 121.32, 120.61, 119.95, 107.46, 103.24,
99.03, 51.57, 29.68, 25.60, 20.93. Anal Calcd for C73H54N4O4: C, 83.40,
H, 5.18, N, 5.33; found: C, 83.15, H, 5.17, N, 5.06. HR-MS(ESI) for
C73H54N4O4·H+ : calcd: 1051.4223; found: 1051.4182.
